# Task 11 – Implement, Test and Defend the Design

## Objective
To implement and test a parking ticket system using Java.

## Implementation
The program creates parking tickets and stores active tickets
in a HashMap using vehicle registration numbers as keys.

## Test Cases

| Test | Expected Result |
|---|---|
| Add two vehicles | 2 active tickets |
| Search for a registered vehicle | Vehicle found |
| Remove a vehicle on exit | 1 active ticket remains |
| Search for an unknown vehicle | Vehicle not found |

## Complexity Analysis

Array:
- Searching for a ticket: O(n).
- Space: O(n).

ArrayList:
- Searching for a ticket: O(n).
- Removing a ticket: O(n).
- Space: O(n).

HashMap:
- Searching for a ticket: O(1) average.
- Removing a ticket: O(1) average.
- Space: O(n).

## Evaluation
A HashMap provides efficient searching and removal using
vehicle registration numbers. Duplicate registrations should
be checked before adding a new ticket.

## Limitation
The example uses a simplified parking fee calculation and
does not include complete floor and slot allocation.

## Conclusion
A HashMap is suitable for managing active parking tickets
because it provides efficient average-case lookup.